       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because 30 mg is above the usual limit for amlodipine. The maximum recommended adult dose is 10 mg once daily. 30 mg is three times that, and it raises the risk of severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) would justify a dose that high.\n\nDid you mean a different dose? The usual options are:\n- **2.5 mg PO daily:** a starting dose for frail or elderly patients, or for patients with hepatic impairment.\n- **5 mg PO daily:** the standard starting dose.\n- **10 mg PO daily:** the maximum dose.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 30 mg is intentional, for example as part of a plan I don't have, please confirm that with your supervising resident or attending and with pharmacy. Then tell me, and I can enter it with a note recording that it was verified."
      }
