       "text": "I'm not going to enter this one as written. Your confirmation doesn't change my concern. You're a student, and I asked for the dose to be checked with your resident, attending, or pharmacy. A dose of 30 mg is three times the maximum, and it could cause serious harm if it's wrong. A second check is cheap, and an error here could be dangerous.\n\nHere are two ways to move forward:\n1. **Enter a standard dose now.** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg PO once daily, and your team can titrate from there.\n2. **Enter 30 mg after it's verified.** Once your attending or a pharmacist has explicitly approved it, tell me who approved it and I'll enter the order with that in the note. Many hospital systems will also require the supervising prescriber to enter or co-sign an order like this.\n\nWhich would you like?"
